# Summary

The statute's retention rule states that records are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute. [[cite:obs-89a70526afa3e2f9ea209ebc87e4adef9ed88ce5 "Records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute."]]

The schedule specifies that ledgers are kept for eleven calendar years and then shredded. [[cite:obs-b504388369b34536a5bf094ea1a0a33e73fe15b0 "Ledgers: eleven calendar years, shredding afterwards."]]